			"Message": "build(Cocoon): Migrate ESBuild configuration to PascalCase and unminify build artifacts\n\nRefactor the ESBuild configuration system within `Configuration/ESBuild/` to align with the project's PascalCase naming convention. Rename default imports from `i`, `d`, `f` to explicit identifiers like `default2`, `default3`, and `default4`. Introduce clearly named constants `CocoonESBuildConfig`, `CocoonESBuildDevConfig`, and `CocoonESBuildProdConfig` to replace ambiguous variable assignments.\n\nUpdate `BaseConfig.js` to import environment constants explicitly from `Constant/EnvironmentConstant.js` rather than relying on implicit globals, ensuring `On`, `Clean`, and `Bundle` states are correctly resolved. Modify `MountainConfig.js` to rename functions (`loadMountainConfigFromEnv`, `validateMountainConfig`, `createMountainConfig`, `getMountainConfigSummary`) and add detailed validation logic for TLS and connection parameters.\n\nDisable minification and enable source maps for the production build to facilitate debugging of the generated `Target/` artifacts, which now include full stack traces for all services including `RPCServer`, `FileSystemRoute`, and `TypeConverter`. Update the `RouteManifest` generation timestamp and refine comments in `FileSystemRoute.ts` for clarity on URI parsing.\n\nThis change ensures the build configuration is maintainable and the output artifacts are debuggable while adhering to strict naming standards.",
			"SHA": "5c0683628fa0415b265e1e71c838bd0a4ddc8457"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T07:23:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				648,
				84
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Integrate OTLP tracing and production-safe telemetry gating\n\nIntroduce `OTLPBridge` for fire-and-forget Jaeger span emission, wired into `PostHogBridge` to stamp `$trace_id` on all events. This enables end-to-end visibility into extension-host latency and handler dispatch times via the Feature Parity dashboard.\n\nRefactor telemetry initialization to use dynamic imports gated by `process.env.NODE_ENV`. Esbuild's `define` substitution ensures the entire PostHog and OTLP pathways are dead-coded in production builds, shipping zero telemetry overhead to the final bundle. Apply this pattern across `CocoonMain.ts`, `RequestRoutingHandler.ts`, and `WrapNamespaceWithHeuristics.ts`.\n\nCleanup build configuration by un-minifying ESBuild constants and ensuring `MountainConfig` validation logic remains intact. Update `CHANGELOG.md` to document the v2.2 correctness pass and v2.1 namespace split.",
			"SHA": "a980130af44c4dcb01af83334e339a83fb07ae28"
		},
